es` refusal case was malformed JSON\n57|  (refused on shape, never reached ordering). Replaced with a genuinely\n58|  descending valid pair built via `joinUnsortedForTest`.\n59|\n60|## Mutation evidence (refreshed this run, exact-source)\n61|\n62|- `.temp/TASK-260909-2ez769/mutations-hosttrust/`: 15 narrowing mutants\n63|  KILLED by named tests + 1 neutral SURVIVED control (`results.json`,\n64|  `table.md`, `manifest.json` with current source digests). New probes:\n65|  digest-root-swap, unique-root-pair, retire-expiry, custody-binding.\n66|  The old `>=`-to-`>` sort mutant stopped killing once the mapping gate\n67|  subsumed identical entries; re-aimed to `==` (admits unsorted-but-distinct)\n68|  and kills via the genuine unsorted fixture.\n69|- `.temp/TASK-260909-2ez769/mutations-config/`: rerun, 4 narrowing KILLED +\n70|  1 neutral passed (config source unchanged).\n71|- No gate searches source text for a token (all gates operate on decoded\n72|  values/DER/parsed TOML); the preserve-token behavioral-mutant clause is\n73|  vacuous here, as previously stated.\n74|\n75|## Gates rerun by this run (all exit 0)\n76|\n77|- `gofmt` clean; `go build ./...` 0; `go vet` on\n78|  hosttrust/config/peeridentity/secprim 0.\n79|- `go test ./... -count=1` all ok; `go test ./... -cover` all ok\n80|  (hosttrust 77.0%, config 93.2%, peeridentity 97.5%, secprim 94.4%).\n81|  Includes secprim census and config refusal-inventory audit.\n82|\n83|## Accepted from attached evidence (unchanged code, not rerun)\n84|\n85|- Prior `TASK-260909-2ez769_results.md` 21/21 AC-rows-driven accounting for\n86|  the pre-existing implementation (reader, enrollment, rotation, revocation,\n87|  generation authz, custody, preview/apply/rollback, preservation, stated\n88|  bounds for live TLS/dispatch/stream lifecycle owned by the RPC task,\n89|  Windows DACL beyond owner checks, peer-side distribution as operator duty).\n90|  This run's additions extend the reader/rotation/custody rows; the ratio\n91|  ac